{{Quote|Bloodshed is bad for business. This can be dealt with later. Sleep lightly, bounty hunter.|translated=1|The Hutt brother, to Boba Fett|<ref name="Chapter 2" />}}
A '''Hutt''' [[Gender|male]], alongside his [[twin]] [[Unidentified Hutt sister|sister]], attempted to claim [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]]'s [[Jabba's criminal empire|criminal empire]] after the [[death]] of [[Bib Fortuna]]. However, [[Boba Fett]]&mdash;the new [[Daimyo]] of [[Mos Espa]]&mdash;claimed Jabba's territory for [[Fett gotra|his own empire]], putting him in conflict with the [[Hutt]] [[The Twins|siblings]] from [[Nal Hutta]].

==Biography==
{{Quote|The Twins have laid claim to their late cousin's bequest.''"<br />"''The Twins are preoccupied with the debauchery of Hutta to bother with any ambitions on Tatooine.|Garsa Fwip and Boba Fett|<ref name="Chapter 2" />}}
[[File:Hutt_Twins.png|thumb|left|250px|The Hutt brother and his twin sister were cousins of the late Jabba Desilijic Tiure.]]
The [[Hutt]] [[Gender|male]] was a cousin of [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]], the [[crime lord]] who controlled the [[city]] of [[Mos Espa]] on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]] until his [[Rescue of Han Solo|demise]]<ref name="Chapter 2" /> in [[4 ABY]].<ref name="GA">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> The Hutt and his [[twin]] [[Unidentified Hutt sister|sister]] were collectively known as "[[the Twins]];" they originally resided on [[Nal Hutta]]<ref name="Chapter 2" />&mdash;the [[homeworld]] of the Hutt [[species]]<ref name="Nal Hutta DB">{{Databank|nal-hutta|Nal Hutta}}</ref>&mdash;prior to their move to Tatooine<ref name="Chapter 2" /> around [[9 ABY]].<ref name="9 ABY">{{BoBFDate}}</ref> Their claim over [[Jabba's criminal empire|Jabba's territory]] conflicted with the agenda of [[Boba Fett]], the self-proclaimed [[Daimyo]] of Mos Espa, who sought to build his own [[Fett gotra|criminal empire]] after [[Attack on Jabba's Palace (Boba Fett)|killing]] [[Bib Fortuna]].<ref name="Chapter 2" />

Accompanied by their servants and the [[Wookiee]] [[gladiator]] [[Krrsantan]], the Twins met with Fett and [[Fennec Shand]] outside of [[Garsa Fwip]]'s [[cantina]], the [[Garsa Fwip's Sanctuary|Sanctuary]], and publicly declared their intention to take control of Mos Espa. Fett rejected the assertion that the Twins were the legitimate inheritors of Jabba's legacy, and presented himself as the rightful crime [[lord]] on Tatooine. While the Hutt sister desired to [[Death|kill]] the former [[bounty hunter]] immediately, the Hutt brother decided to settle the dispute with Fett at a later point in [[time]].<ref name="Chapter 2" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|You've upset my sister. I'm more patient than she is.|translated=1|The Hutt brother, to Boba Fett|<ref name="Chapter 2" />}}
[[File:The-Twins-Hutts-Boba-Espa.png|thumb|right|250px|The Hutt brother traveled in comfort on a litter carried by servants.]]
Contrary to the opinion of Boba Fett, who believed that the Twins were too distracted by a life of "debauchery" on Nal Hutta to pursue their ambitions on Tatooine, the Hutt brother journeyed to the remote desert world alongside his sister with the intention of claiming the dominion of their late cousin, Jabba Desilijic Tiure. Whereas Fett had chosen to eschew the outward signs of power as a crime lord, the Hutt brother and his sister traveled in comfort, riding together on a double-wide litter supported by servants and using [[drum]]s to announce their arrival to the population of Mos Espa. In addition to the litter, the Hutt brother used a [[rodent]] to wipe sweat off of his face.<ref name="Chapter 2" />

The Hutt brother believed himself and his sister to be the true beneficiaries of their cousin's estate. He refuted Fett's claim that Mos Espa was his territory by presenting a document to confirm Jabba's authority over the city. Possessing more patience than his sister, who wanted to kill Fett after he had upset her, the brother decided to settle their disagreement at a later date, observing that bloodshed was "bad for business."<ref name="Chapter 2" />

The brother twin was a large Hutt with [[Color|orange]] [[eye]]s, green and tan skin, and a facial [[tattoo]]. He spoke [[Huttese]]&mdash;the [[language]] of the Hutts&mdash;and understood [[Galactic Basic Standard]].<ref name="Chapter 2" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|It was pretty much those two guys, without the voiceover, of course. The voiceover came from my wonderful stand-in, a guy called Jimmy. ''[&hellip;]'' He could do all the voices while we were acting.|Temuera Morrison, speaking about the Twins' on-set presence|<ref name="TVLine Hutt Secrets">{{YouTube|video=MHXH73CHK2g|text='Book of Boba Fett' &#124; Temuera Morrison and Ming-Na Wen Talk Episode 2, Hutt Secrets, More|channel=UCL4NqoTi6xcQT4IzUzBwsLg|name=TVLine}}</ref>}}
[[File:HuttTwins-TBoBFPoster.png|thumb|right|200px|The Twins character poster for ''The Book of Boba Fett''.]]
The Hutt brother first appeared in the episode "[[Chapter 2: The Tribes of Tatooine]]" of the [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: The Book of Boba Fett]]''<ref name="Chapter 2" /> on [[January 5]], [[2022]].<ref name="Tribes of Tatooine release date">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-january-2022|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in January 2022}}</ref> According to the [[Wikipedia:Simplified Chinese|Simplified]] and [[Wikipedia:Traditional Chinese|Traditional Chinese]] subtitles of the episode on Disney+, the female Hutt is the male Hutt's younger sister ([[Wiktionary:妹妹|妹妹]], mèimei). The line is spoken in Huttese, regardless of the language a viewer chooses for audio.<ref name="Chapter 2 Mandarin subs">{{BOBF|Chapter 2: The Tribes of Tatooine}} {{C|simplied and traditional Chinese subtitles}}</ref>

According to [[Ming-Na Wen]], cardboard cutouts were used on set to represent the Hutts that would eventually be realized through computer-generated imagery. [[JJ Dashnaw]], the body double of [[Temuera Morrison]], provided dialogue for the Twins during filming.<ref name="TVLine Hutt Secrets" />

